# Dependencies and upstream references

The initial registry check was on 22 September 2026. Alchemy, Effect and the
required Distilled compatibility release were checked again on 8 October 2026.
All direct packages use exact versions or named Bun catalogs; transitive
resolutions are in `bun.lock`.

The pinned native Alchemy release is `2.0.0-beta.81`, with peer `effect ^4.0.0`.
Effect and its matching platform, Atom and test packages use stable `4.0.2`.
These are the latest compatible published releases checked for this upgrade.

The scaffold uses React 19.3.0, TanStack Start 1.168.57, Router 1.170.38,
TypeScript 7.0.2, Vite 8.3.0, Vitest 5.0.1, Oxlint 1.85.0,
@effect/tsgo 0.45.0, Oxfmt 0.70.0 and Bun 1.4.2. The root manifest owns the
complete version list. Vitest 5 satisfies @effect/vitest's current peer range.

## Compatibility decisions

- `@effect/atom-react` 4.0.2 (checked 8 October 2026) is in the `effect`
  catalog at `effect`'s exact version. Its published peer range is
  `scheduler >=0.25.0 <0.28.0`, but React 19.3.0's `react-dom` requires
  `scheduler ^0.28.0`, and the Effect repository develops the package against
  `scheduler ^0.28.0`, so the range looks stale. Bun resolves one `scheduler`
  (0.28.0) and warns about the peer; we accept the warning. It uses the package
  only for `RegistryProvider` and `useAtomMount`. Retire the decision when a
  release widens the range. Stable 4.0.2 retains the same published peer range.

- @effect/tsgo 0.45.0 patches Oxlint 1.81/1.82 only. Keep current Oxlint 1.85
  and run `effect-tsgo diagnostics` separately with the Effect plugin explicitly
  enabled in tsconfig. Do not use `--skip-missing` to hide absent checks.
- `skipLibCheck` applies only to external declaration files. Current Alchemy
  declarations reference optional SQL drivers and Cloudflare globals, and have
  an exact-optional-property mismatch in `DeletingResourceState`. Transitive
  capnp-es also has an exact-optional-property mismatch. We do not install unused
  database drivers or weaken strict checks on owned source to work around them.
  Owned code retains strict mode, exact optional properties and checked indexing.
- Alchemy 2.0.0-beta.81 and its Cloudflare SDK 1.0.0-rc.13 are unpatched.
  Every hosted Preview stage owns ordinary Website/API Workers, whose declared
  observability is supported natively. This removes the Preview-observability
  patches; the completed one-time Worker rename no longer needs its patch.
  No dependency upgrade, custom resource or provider write replaces them.

## Stable Effect and native secrets — 8 October 2026

Cooper authorised the dependency upgrade and full configuration cutover.
All root stacks now use native Doppler followed by optional `.env`, with shell
settings disabled. `.env` overrides Doppler in every environment. The
[deployment runbook](../runbooks/deployment.md#credentials-and-stages) owns the
stage/config mapping, local profile setup and existing scoped CI service tokens.

Stable Effect publishes HTTP, HTTP API, RPC, reactivity, AI and process modules
without `unstable` in their paths. The HTTP API path is `effect/http-api`.
Owned imports and lint recognition follow those exports. Base64 and Hex use
`effect/encoding/Base64` and `effect/encoding/Hex`; the length check is
`Schema.isBetweenLength`. The native error factory remains `Schema.TaggedError`.
The reference tag check accepts stable Effect tags as well as the previous RC
format; source clones stay clean and locked.

The Effect MCP Origin patch and Distilled dashboard PATCH patch retain the
existing behaviour in their new package versions. Their removal remains the
separate accepted design below. No additional provider implementation was copied.

Current reference pins:

- Effect `effect@4.0.2`: `269a7c864351231d42e6e95b7fa8f32050df3691`.
- Alchemy `v2.0.0-beta.81`: `e73c66857553a5abe045e1a66b5512cf7d39ef2e`.

## Reference maintenance

`reference-repositories.json` locks both official Git URLs, tags, commits and
package versions. `bun run references:sync` clones missing sources and verifies
clean, detached checkouts, exact origins, commits and manifest versions. It
refuses symlinks or dirty work and disables Git hooks. It never executes code
from a clone. `references:refresh` fetches the locked tags again, without moving
to an unreviewed main branch.

For an upgrade, inspect current npm metadata and release notes, update the
catalog and reference lock together, run the reference sync, install and run
all checks. Inspect the current Alchemy Cloudflare TanStack example before
changing the deployment. Do not copy Site's older patterns automatically.

The reference decoder requires exactly one Effect entry and one Alchemy entry,
in either order. Each entry owns its official URL and package-manifest path;
its tag must match its version. Repository URLs are branded, including Git
origin readback. The decoder rejects extra fields using explicit parse options
(the installed Effect version does not enforce these through annotations).
Focused Schema tests cover valid round-trips and rejected lockfile shapes.

